C++20 concept evaluation via requires-expressions ([expr.prim.req],
[temp.names]/9).  A concept whose constraint-expression is a requires-expression
(simple-requirement and type-requirement) is evaluated to a constexpr bool, and
a concept-id is used as a non-type bool template argument.  Guards the
front-end concept-evaluation support; see
doc/architectural/cpp-requires-expression-support.md.

Not yet covered (tracked separately): compound-requirements with a
return-type-requirement ({E} -> C) -- blocked on value-category (lvalue)
tracking for decltype((E)); member-call requirements; uniform soft-failure for
requirement forms the parser routes outside the requirement-node handlers.
